    <bpmn:process id="W_W1223" name="W1223. Store-Level Emergency Generator Operations &amp; Extended Power Outage Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Commercial power failure at store location; or brownout announced by electric utility; or generator automatic transfer switch (ATS) activates
Frequency: 4–8 power outages per store per month in provincial areas; 1–2 per month in Metro Manila; extended outages (&gt; 4 hours) ~2–4 times per year per store
Volume: 200 stores × ~50 outage events/year (including brief flickers) = ~10,000 generator activations/year; extended outages affecting 20–50 stores simultaneously during grid failures
Owner: Maintenance/Utility Staff
Participants: Maintenance/Utility Staff, Store Manager, IT Helpdesk, Facilities Maintenance, Electric Utility Customer Service
Source: workflow W1223 — Store-Level Emergency Generator Operations &amp; Extended Power Outage Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1223_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1223_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1223_Lane2" name="Maintenance Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1223_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1223_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1223_Start5" name="Commercial power failure at store location; or brownout announced by electric utility; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1223_Task6" name="Power failure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Power failure: ATS detects commercial power loss and automatically starts generator; generator reaches operating speed and transfers load within 10–30 seconds; if ATS fails to auto-start: Maintenance Staff manually starts generator per posted emergency procedure
Responsible (R): System / Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated (10–30 sec)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1223_Task7" name="generator startup check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Maintenance Staff performs generator startup check: (a) verify generator is running and producing power, (b) check generator control panel for warning lights or fault codes, (c) confirm essential loads powered: POS systems, lighting (minimum 50%), CCTV and security, paint area refrigeration; (d) confirm non-essential loads shed: air conditioning (most units), decorative lighting, non-critical equipment
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1223_Task8" name="Store Manager assesses customer impact: (a) if outage during store hours…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Store Manager assesses customer impact: (a) if outage during store hours: announce to customers via PA system that store remains operational on generator power; apologize for reduced air conditioning; (b) reduce POS terminals to 2 (from 3) to manage generator load; (c) if outage during non-store hours: no customer impact; generator maintains security systems and refrigeration
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1223_Task9" name="Fuel monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fuel monitoring (if outage extends beyond 2 hours): Maintenance Staff checks generator fuel gauge: (a) full tank provides ~8–12 hours at essential load, (b) if outage projected to exceed 8 hours: Maintenance Staff contacts Facilities Maintenance for emergency fuel delivery per W913, (c) Store Manager implements fuel conservation: reduce lighting to emergency-only, pause paint refrigeration cycling (short-term acceptable), reduce POS terminals to 1
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Facilities Maintenance
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1223_Task10" name="Extended outage management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Extended outage management (&gt; 4 hours): (a) Store Manager contacts electric utility for estimated restoration time; (b) if restoration &gt; 12 hours: Store Manager considers early store closure (revenue loss vs. fuel cost and customer comfort); (c) if restoration &gt; 24 hours: Regional Manager authorizes store closure; Maintenance Staff configures generator for security-only load (CCTV, alarm, lighting) to conserve fuel; (d) IT Helpdesk monitors POS offline status — if offline approaching 8-hour threshold per W5G, Store Manager executes offline POS procedure
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1223_Task11" name="Power restoration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Power restoration: ATS detects commercial power return; (a) ATS automatically transfers load back to commercial power after 5-minute stability verification, (b) generator runs cooldown cycle (5 min unloaded) then shuts down, (c) Maintenance Staff verifies: all systems on commercial power, POS terminals restored to full operation, air conditioning restarts, no equipment damage from power transition
Responsible (R): System / Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1223_Task12" name="Post-outage report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-outage report: Maintenance Staff logs outage event in system: (a) date/time of outage, (b) duration, (c) cause (if known from utility), (d) generator run hours, (e) fuel consumed, (f) any equipment issues during generator operation, (g) any revenue impact (early closure); Facilities Maintenance aggregates data monthly to identify stores with frequent/long outages for generator upgrade or UPS consideration
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff / Facilities Maintenance
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1223_Task13" name="Monthly generator maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly generator maintenance: Maintenance Staff conducts: (a) visual inspection for leaks, corrosion, belt wear, (b) check oil level and coolant level, (c) test-start generator under load for 30 min (scheduled during non-store hours), (d) log run hours and schedule preventive maintenance per manufacturer intervals (every 250 run hours or 6 months), (e) verify fuel quality (diesel degrades over time — treat with biocide if stored &gt; 6 months)
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff / Generator Vendor
Accountable (A): Facilities Maintenance
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1223_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1223_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1223_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1223_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-314 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Preparedness (PA-24.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Maintenance/Utility Staff</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1223_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1223_Annotation15" targetRef="W1223_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1223_Flow17" sourceRef="W1223_Start5" targetRef="W1223_Task6" />
