    <bpmn:process id="W_W1296" name="W1296. Store-Level Fire Safety Equipment Inspection &amp; BFP Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly fire safety equipment inspection cycle; or annual BFP (Bureau of Fire Protection) inspection schedule
Frequency: Monthly self-inspection; annual BFP inspection per location
Volume: 200 stores + 4 DCs + 1 HQ = 205 locations; ~15–20 fire safety devices per location
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Maintenance/Utility, Department Supervisors, BFP Inspector
Source: workflow W1296 — Store-Level Fire Safety Equipment Inspection &amp; BFP Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1296_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1296_Lane1" name="Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1296_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1296_Lane3" name="Department Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1296_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1296_Start5" name="Monthly fire safety equipment inspection cycle; or annual BFP (Bureau of Fire Protection)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1296_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1296_Task6" name="Monthly fire safety equipment inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly fire safety equipment inspection: Maintenance/Utility conducts monthly inspection of all fire safety equipment: (a) fire extinguishers: check pressure gauge (green zone), inspection tag date, hose condition, pin and tamper seal intact, no visible corrosion; count and verify location matches floor plan (fire extinguisher within 23 meters of travel distance per NFPA 10, adopted by BFP), (b) fire alarm system: test call points (1 per zone monthly rotation), verify alarm sounds and strobes activate, check control panel for faults, (c) emergency lighting and exit signs: test battery backup by simulating power failure, verify exit signs illuminated, (d) sprinkler system (if installed): check pressure gauge, valve positions, no obstructions within 45 cm of sprinkler heads, (e) fire exit paths: verify exits unobstructed, self-closing doors functional, panic hardware operational
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 60 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1296_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1296_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1296_Task7" name="Inspection documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Inspection documentation: Maintenance/Utility records inspection results in fire safety log (physical logbook and digital form in ERP): (a) date, inspector name, equipment ID, location, condition (pass/fail), corrective action needed, (b) photo documentation of any deficiencies, (c) for failed items: create maintenance request per W269 with &quot;Fire Safety — Urgent&quot; priority, (d) system tracks inspection compliance rate per location (target: 100% monthly completion)
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1296_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1296_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1296_Task8" name="Corrective maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Corrective maintenance: For failed equipment: (a) Maintenance/Utility performs in-house repair if capable (replace extinguisher hose, replace emergency light battery, clear obstructed exit), (b) for items requiring external service: engage fire safety vendor (extinguisher refilling, sprinkler maintenance, alarm system repair) per service contract, (c) target resolution: within 7 days for non-critical items, within 24 hours for critical items (inoperative fire extinguisher in high-risk area, blocked fire exit), (d) verify repair by re-inspection and update fire safety log
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility / Vendor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per issue</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1296_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1296_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1296_Task9" name="Annual BFP inspection preparation (T-30 days)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Annual BFP inspection preparation (T-30 days): Store Manager prepares for annual BFP inspection: (a) review year&#x27;s fire safety inspection logs for completeness, (b) ensure all corrective actions resolved and documented, (c) verify FSIC application documents: building floor plan with fire exits marked, fire safety equipment inventory, evacuation plan, fire drill records per W445, (d) verify Fire Safety Conformance Certificate (FSCC) is current for building, (e) conduct pre-inspection walkthrough simulating BFP inspector&#x27;s checklist, (f) brief all staff on inspection protocol and fire safety awareness
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1296_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1296_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1296_Task10" name="BFP inspection day">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: BFP inspection day: BFP fire inspector conducts inspection: (a) Store Manager accompanies inspector, (b) inspector checks: fire extinguisher placement and condition, fire exit accessibility and signage, fire alarm system functionality, emergency lighting, sprinkler system (if applicable), electrical safety (no overloaded circuits, proper wiring in paint mixing area), storage of flammable materials (paint, solvents per W492), occupancy load compliance, fire drill records, (c) inspector issues findings: &quot;Compliant&quot; (FSIC issued) or &quot;Non-Compliant&quot; with list of deficiencies and correction period
Responsible (R): Store Manager / BFP Inspector
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1296_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1296_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1296_Task11" name="BFP deficiency resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: BFP deficiency resolution: If BFP issues deficiencies: (a) Store Manager creates corrective action plan with timeline per BFP requirements, (b) resolve all deficiencies within correction period (typically 15–30 days), (c) request BFP re-inspection upon completion, (d) if FSIC is a prerequisite for LGU business permit renewal per W54: escalate timeline to Regional Manager to avoid permit lapse, (e) submit resolution documentation to BFP for FSIC issuance
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: Per deficiency</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1296_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1296_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1296_Task12" name="Fire safety training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Fire safety training: Quarterly, Department Supervisors conduct fire safety refresher for all staff: (a) fire extinguisher operation (PASS technique: Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep), (b) evacuation routes and assembly points, (c) fire alarm activation and emergency notification procedure, (d) specific risks in assigned area (paint department: chemical fire; lumber yard: combustible materials; electrical: electrical fire), (e) document attendance in training system per W614
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1296_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1296_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1296_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1296_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1296_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-314 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Preparedness (PA-24.2).) | - operational: internal inspection held to the highest BFP standard, with retrofit tracking where required for FSIC renewal
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
