    <bpmn:process id="W_W1386" name="W1386. Typhoon Early Warning Response, Store Pre-Closure Preparation &amp; Post-Disaster Assessment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA (Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration) raises Tropical Cyclone Wind Signal (TCWS) Signal No. 3 or higher in a province where BuildRight has stores or DCs; or Signal No. 2 with forecast trajectory indicating intensification
Frequency: ~8–12 typhoon events/year affecting BuildRight operations (Philippine average: 20 typhoons/year; BuildRight&#x27;s footprint covers Mindanao, Visayas, Luzon, NCR)
Volume: Per event: 10–50 stores and 1–2 DCs may be affected depending on typhoon path and size
Owner: VP Store Operations (store response); DC Operations Manager (DC response)
Participants: VP Store Operations, DC Operations Manager, Regional Managers, Store Managers, Facilities Manager, Safety Officer, Insurance Coordinator, HR Manager, Communications Manager
Source: workflow W1386 — Typhoon Early Warning Response, Store Pre-Closure Preparation &amp; Post-Disaster Assessment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1386_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1386_Lane1" name="Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1386_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1386_Lane3" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1386_Lane4" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1386_Lane5" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1386_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1386_Start7" name="PAGASA (Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1386_Task8" name="Early warning monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Early warning monitoring: Safety Officer monitors PAGASA bulletins every 3 hours during active typhoon events; COO receives automated alerts when TCWS Signal is raised in any province with BuildRight locations; system maps affected stores and DCs based on location master
Responsible (R): Safety Officer / System
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Ongoing during events</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task9" name="TCWS Signal 1–2 activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: TCWS Signal 1–2 activation: (a) Store Manager reviews store preparedness checklist: sandbags positioned at entry points, outdoor lumber yard materials secured or moved indoors, display fixtures on exterior walls moved away from windows, loose signage and banners removed; (b) DC Operations Manager reviews DC preparedness: dock doors secured, outdoor inventory covered or moved indoors, generator fuel topped up, backup communication equipment tested
Responsible (R): Store Manager / DC Ops Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task10" name="TCWS Signal 3+ activation — pre-closure preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: TCWS Signal 3+ activation — pre-closure preparation: (a) VP Store Operations authorizes pre-emptive store closure for affected locations; (b) Store Manager executes pre-closure protocol: accelerate remaining customer transactions (30 min), secure all cash in safe, shut down POS terminals properly (data sync), move remaining customers and staff to interior of building away from windows, seal doors and windows; (c) DC Operations Manager halts all inbound/outbound operations; secures all inventory in racking; activates warehouse emergency lighting; non-essential staff released to go home early
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Store Manager / DC Ops Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 hours/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task11" name="During typhoon (shelter-in-place or closure)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: During typhoon (shelter-in-place or closure): (a) essential personnel only at DC (security, facilities); (b) stores closed and locked; (c) Safety Officer monitors PAGASA and NDRRMC (National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council) advisories; (d) Communications Manager sends employee safety advisories via SMS/WhatsApp group; (e) COO maintains situation room with affected store/DC status dashboard
Responsible (R): Safety Officer / VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task12" name="Post-typhoon all-clear">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-typhoon all-clear (PAGASA lowers TCWS or issues all-clear): (a) Store Manager or DC Operations Manager conducts initial visual assessment (when safe to travel): structural integrity (roof, walls, windows, doors), flooding level, power status, access road conditions; (b) reports assessment via standardized damage assessment form (mobile app): green (no damage, ready to open), yellow (minor damage, can open with temporary fixes), red (significant damage, cannot open until repairs); (c) photographs all damage for insurance documentation per W610
Responsible (R): Store Manager / DC Ops Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–3 hours/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task13" name="Recovery prioritization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Recovery prioritization: COO reviews damage assessments from all affected locations; prioritizes recovery: (a) DCs first (supply chain must resume); (b) top-revenue stores; (c) stores serving as community supply points (building materials needed for community recovery); (d) coordinates with Facilities Manager for contractor dispatch for emergency repairs
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task14" name="Insurance notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Insurance notification: within 24 hours of damage discovery, Insurance Coordinator notifies property insurance carrier of damage claims per W610; preliminary damage estimate provided; adjuster site visit scheduled
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 hour/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task15" name="Inventory damage assessment and write-off">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Inventory damage assessment and write-off: for damaged inventory, Store Manager / DC Ops Manager works with Inventory Accountant to: (a) identify damaged SKUs and quantities; (b) photograph damage; (c) system writes off damaged inventory (Dr. Inventory Loss / Cr. Inventory); (d) damaged goods segregated for insurance adjuster inspection before disposal
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Inventory Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4–8 hours/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task16" name="Employee welfare check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Employee welfare check: HR Manager coordinates welfare check for all employees at affected locations — confirms safety, assesses personal property damage, provides emergency assistance (advance salary, emergency loan, or company relief goods) per company policy
Responsible (R): HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–4 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task17" name="Reopening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Reopening: Store Manager reopens when: (a) structural safety confirmed, (b) power restored (or generator operational), (c) POS system operational, (d) minimum staffing available (at least 10 employees), (e) adequate inventory on hand for meaningful sales; Store Manager confirms reopening to Regional Manager and COO
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1386_Task18" name="Post-event review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Post-event review: within 2 weeks of event, COO conducts lessons-learned review: (a) adequacy of pre-closure timing, (b) damage patterns and structural vulnerabilities, (c) recovery speed vs. RTO targets per W847 BCP, (d) insurance claim processing speed, (e) employee communication effectiveness; updates preparedness checklist and BCP as needed
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1386_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1386_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1386_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1386_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-314 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Preparedness (PA-24.2).) | - operational: VP Store Operations (store response); DC Operations Manager (DC response) review and approval gate
Owner: VP Store Operations (store response); DC Operations Manager (DC response)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1386_Assoc21" sourceRef="W1386_Annotation20" targetRef="W1386_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
