    <bpmn:process id="W_W1387" name="W1387. Store-Level Flood Response, Inventory Elevation Protocol &amp; Water Damage Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA heavy rainfall warning (Red Rainfall Advisory) or localized flooding observed at store (water entering building, parking lot flooding, adjacent creek/river overflow)
Frequency: ~5–10 flood events/year affecting individual stores (localized); ~1–3 major flood events/year affecting multiple stores (regional)
Volume: Per event: 1–20 stores may experience flooding; flood depth varies from 5 cm (parking lot) to 100+ cm (ground floor)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Stock Associates, Facilities Technician, Insurance Coordinator, Inventory Accountant, Regional Manager
Source: workflow W1387 — Store-Level Flood Response, Inventory Elevation Protocol &amp; Water Damage Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1387_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1387_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1387_Lane2" name="Stock Associates">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1387_Lane3" name="Inventory Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1387_Lane4" name="Facilities Tech">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1387_Lane5" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1387_Lane6" name="Facilities Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1387_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1387_Start8" name="PAGASA heavy rainfall warning (Red Rainfall Advisory) or localized flooding observed at…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1387_Task9" name="Flood warning activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Flood warning activation: Store Manager receives automated heavy rainfall alert from PAGASA for store&#x27;s municipality/city; monitors local LGU (Local Government Unit) flood advisories and social media for real-time flood reports from nearby areas
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Continuous during events</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1387_Task10" name="Preventive inventory elevation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Preventive inventory elevation (when warning issued and flood risk is probable): Store Manager activates flood response protocol: (a) Priority 1 — Floor-level inventory: Stock Associates move bottom-shelf merchandise to upper shelves or pallets (minimum 30 cm elevation); focus on water-sensitive categories: cement, plywood, MDF boards, electrical supplies (wire, switches, breakers), paint, plumbing fixtures, power tools in original packaging; (b) Priority 2 — Outdoor lumber yard: move lumber, plywood, and steel bars to covered area or elevate on blocks; cover with tarpaulins; (c) Priority 3 — Low-value/high-volume items: sandbags, gravel bags, hollow blocks — leave in place (cost of moving exceeds damage risk); (d) target: complete elevation within 2 hours of warning
Responsible (R): Stock Associates / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2 hours (all hands)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1387_Task11" name="During flooding">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: During flooding (if water enters building): (a) Store Manager orders evacuation of customers and non-essential staff to upper floor or safe area; (b) electrical mains shut off to prevent electrocution risk; (c) POS systems powered down properly (data sync); (d) cash secured in upper-floor safe; (e) staff shelter in safe interior area
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1387_Task12" name="Post-flood assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-flood assessment (when water recedes and LGU declares safe): Store Manager conducts damage assessment: (a) water depth markers recorded at multiple points in store and lumber yard; (b) photograph all affected areas with GPS timestamp; (c) identify damaged inventory — categories, SKUs, quantities, damage type (submerged, water-splashed, humidity-damaged packaging); (d) identify damaged fixtures and equipment (shelving, display units, refrigeration for paint, forklifts if DC); (e) assess structural damage (floor heaving, wall water damage, electrical system contamination)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Facilities Tech
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1387_Task13" name="Inventory damage processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Inventory damage processing: Inventory Accountant processes damaged inventory in system: (a) create inventory damage report with SKU, quantity, unit cost, total damage value; (b) segregate damaged goods in roped-off area — do not dispose until insurance adjuster inspection (W610); (c) for goods that can be salvaged (e.g., cement bags with only outer packaging wet, lumber with surface water only): quality inspection by Department Supervisor; if structurally sound, re-label and sell as &quot;open box&quot; or at discount; (d) system writes off unsalvageable inventory: Dr. Inventory Loss — Flood / Cr. Inventory
Responsible (R): Inventory Accountant / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4–8 hours/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1387_Task14" name="Cleaning and restoration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Cleaning and restoration: (a) Facilities Technician coordinates professional water damage restoration: extract standing water, industrial dehumidifiers, anti-mold treatment for walls and floors, electrical system inspection and re-certification; (b) Store Manager coordinates cleaning crew for floor scrubbing, shelf cleaning, and re-merchandising; (c) target: store operational within 24–48 hours for minor flooding (&lt; 10 cm), 3–7 days for major flooding (&gt; 30 cm)
Responsible (R): Facilities Tech / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–7 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1387_Task15" name="Insurance claim">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Insurance claim: Insurance Coordinator files flood damage claim per W610 — property damage (building, fixtures) + inventory loss + business interruption (lost sales during closure); provides damage assessment documentation, photographs, and inventory write-off report
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–4 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1387_Task16" name="Post-flood preventive measures">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-flood preventive measures: for stores with recurring flood history (2+ floods in 3 years), Facilities Manager evaluates: (a) install flood barriers at entry points, (b) elevate electrical panels and POS terminals above historical flood level, (c) reconfigure lowest shelving to use only for water-resistant merchandise (PVC pipes, metal hardware), (d) install sump pumps in low-lying areas, (e) negotiate lease amendment with landlord for flood-resilient building improvements (if leased per W117)
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–8 hours/recurring location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1387_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1387_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1387_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1387_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-314 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Preparedness (PA-24.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1387_Assoc19" sourceRef="W1387_Annotation18" targetRef="W1387_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
