    <bpmn:process id="W_W5537" name="W5537. Fire Event Response, Suppression &amp; Post-Fire BFP Clearance (Store &amp; DC)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Fire or smoke detected — alarm-panel activation, sprinkler flow switch, staff/customer report, or a lithium-ion battery thermal event at the charging station per W1007&#x27;s risk framing — anywhere in a store&#x27;s 8,000–15,000 sqm footprint, a DC&#x27;s 25,000–40,000 sqm facility, or their yards
Frequency: Rare; ~2–5 incipient (self-extinguished/suppressed) events and &lt; 1 reportable structural fire per year chain-wide
Volume: 1 site × full evacuation population (store: ~467 customers/day + 29 staff; DC: ~120–180 staff/shift) × all fire-load zones (paint/solvents, lumber yard, battery-charging stations, rack storage)
Owner: Store Manager / DC Operations Manager
Participants: Store/DC Manager, all floor/shift staff (sweep &amp; muster roles), Safety Officer, Security Guard, Facilities Coordinator, BFP (first-alarm response), Regional Manager (multi-site escalation), Insurance/BCP (VS-26 W876 claim chain), VP Legal, HSE Manager, POS/Cash Office (W850 cash securing)
Source: workflow W5537 — Fire Event Response, Suppression &amp; Post-Fire BFP Clearance (Store &amp; DC)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5537_LaneSet8">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5537_Lane1" name="Duty Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_Start9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5537_Lane2" name="Facilities Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5537_Lane3" name="All floor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5537_Lane4" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5537_Lane5" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5537_Lane6" name="Structural Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5537_Lane7" name="HSE">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5537_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5537_Start9" name="Fire or smoke detected — alarm-panel activation, sprinkler flow switch, staff/customer…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5537_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5537_Task10" name="Alarm verification &amp; classification (RACE)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Alarm verification &amp; classification (RACE): first staff member / alarm panel signal → Manager classifies: incipient (single detector, contained, e.g. wastebasket or charging-station unit) vs developing (multiple detectors, smoke layering, sprinkler flow switch). Incipient + safe: trained staff attempt first-response extinguishment with portable extinguishers (PASS) only within their training, with a second person and an exit at their back; anything beyond incipient → immediate evacuation branch
Responsible (R): Duty Supervisor / Manager
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: &lt; 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5537_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5537_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5537_Task11" name="Suppression support &amp; utilities isolation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Suppression support &amp; utilities isolation: confirm sprinkler system flowing (never obstruct), close fire doors/shutters, isolate non-essential electrical panels and LPG/cylinder supplies per the site&#x27;s isolation map; DC: halt all MHE and dock operations, rack aisles cleared for BFP access
Responsible (R): Facilities Coordinator / Duty Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: 2–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5537_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5537_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5537_Task12" name="Evacuation &amp; muster">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Evacuation &amp; muster: execute the W695 evacuation protocol — zone sweeps (fitting rooms, restrooms, stockrooms, lumber yard, DC rack aisles), PA script, assembly-point roll call against the shift roster and visitor/contractor log per W696; report any unaccounted person to BFP incident commander immediately with last-seen location
Responsible (R): All floor/shift staff / Safety Officer
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5537_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5537_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5537_Task13" name="BFP coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: BFP coordination: security meets the first-alarm apparatus at the fire-lane entrance with the site keys, Knox box access, chemical-inventory SDS binder (paint/solvents/aerosols), and the fire-protection-system status (riser valves, pump); site manager remains available to the incident commander; no re-entry for salvage until BFP releases the scene
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Manager
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: BFP-led (1–4 hrs)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5537_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5537_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5537_Task14" name="Scene security, salvage &amp; cash protection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Scene security, salvage &amp; cash protection: after fire-scene release, secure the site (boarding, perimeters, guards if overnight), execute W850 cash-securing mechanics if the event interrupted trading, and quarantine smoke/water-damaged stock into damage cases with photographic evidence for claim support per W90&#x27;s evidence standard
Responsible (R): Facilities / LP / Cash Office
Accountable (A): Regional Manager (store) / DC Ops Manager (DC)
Duration: 4–16 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5537_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5537_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5537_Task15" name="Structural assessment &amp; BFP clearance-to-reopen">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Structural assessment &amp; BFP clearance-to-reopen: licensed structural engineer assesses fire-affected structure (rack anchors, roof trusses, mezzanine) before any restocking; BFP conducts post-fire re-inspection; W806 recertifies impaired suppression/detection systems; trading resumes only with written BFP clearance + engineer&#x27;s fit-out report + recertified systems — tracked as a formal gate with Regional Manager sign-off
Responsible (R): Structural Engineer / Safety Officer / BFP
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations (store) / VP Supply Chain (DC)
Duration: 3–14 days elapsed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5537_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5537_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5537_Task16" name="Claim, reporting &amp; review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Claim, reporting &amp; review: initiate the VS-26 W876 property/BI claim with the W90-grade evidence pack; file W140/W436 for any injury; BFP fire-incident report obtained for the file; post-incident review within 10 business days feeding corrective actions into W806/W1296 checklists and the W158 drill program; near-miss/battery-event learnings routed to W1007 and chain-wide if systemic
Responsible (R): HSE / Insurance / Safety Officer
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk (review sign-off)
Duration: 5–10 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5537_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5537_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5537_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5537_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5537_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-314 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Preparedness (PA-24.2).) | - operational: trading resumes only after the three-party reopen gate (BFP clearance + structural sign-off + suppression recertification) is evidenced in the incident case | - operational: first-response extinguishment attempted only by trained staff within the incipient classification, with a second person and a clear exit
Owner: Store Manager / DC Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5537_Assoc19" sourceRef="W5537_Annotation18" targetRef="W5537_Start9" associationDirection="None" />
