    <bpmn:process id="W_W5538" name="W5538. Bomb Threat Response &amp; Search-or-Evacuation Decision Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A bomb threat received against a store, DC, or corporate site by phone call, written note, email, or social-media post — whether credible, vague, or assessed as hoax
Frequency: Rare; ~1–3 threats chain-wide per year (the vast majority hoaxes)
Volume: 1 site × full premises population (store: ~467 customers/day + 29 staff; DC: 120–180 staff/shift) × all zones (sales floor, stockrooms, yards, parking)
Owner: Store Manager / Regional Manager
Participants: Store/DC Manager, Security Guard, trained staff search teams (zone-based), Safety Officer, PNP (911) &amp; PNP-EOD bomb disposal, BFP (standby), VP Legal, Corporate Communications (W855 tree if event escalates), LP (CCTV preservation per W471)
Source: workflow W5538 — Bomb Threat Response &amp; Search-or-Evacuation Decision Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5538_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5538_Lane1" name="Receiving Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5538_Lane2" name="Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5538_Lane3" name="Store">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5538_Lane4" name="All Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5538_Lane5" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5538_Lane6" name="LP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5538_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5538_Start8" name="A bomb threat received against a store, DC, or corporate site by phone call, written…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5538_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5538_Task9" name="Threat intake &amp; recording">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Threat intake &amp; recording: receiving employee uses the bomb-threat data card — exact wording, caller details (accent, background sounds, number display), claimed device location/type/timing, demanded action/deadline; keep the caller talking, do not hang up first; written/electronic threats preserved untouched (bag photos of notes; screenshot emails/posts before any deletion); report to Manager immediately
Responsible (R): Receiving Employee / Manager
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: During call + 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5538_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5538_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5538_Task10" name="Notify &amp; escalate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Notify &amp; escalate: 911/PNP report (regardless of credibility assessment), Regional Manager notified, silent alert to Security and zone-search team leads; radios and mobile phones minimized in the searched area (RF-trigger precaution)
Responsible (R): Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5538_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5538_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5538_Task11" name="Search-or-evacuate decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Search-or-evacuate decision: Manager decides per the two-branch rule — (a) threat with specific placement/timing detail, found suspicious package, or written/graphic threat → immediate evacuation branch (Step 4); (b) vague/generic threat → trained-staff covert sweep of their own work zones (staff search only areas they know: look, do not touch — packages that don&#x27;t belong: out-of-place containers, unattended bags, unusual wiring), 15–20 min sweep; any find at any point → escalate to evacuation + PNP-EOD
Responsible (R): Store/DC Manager (decision) / trained staff (sweep)
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: Decision &lt; 5 min; sweep 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5538_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5538_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5538_Task12" name="Evacuation execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Evacuation execution (if invoked): W695 mechanics with a threat-specific script — PA announcement avoids the words &quot;bomb&quot;/&quot;threat&quot; (e.g. &quot;managers to the floor, please leave your transactions and proceed to the exits&quot;), customers and staff routed to the upwind assembly point ≥ 300 m from the building and beyond the parking perimeter, parking entrances closed to inbound traffic, cash-left-in-drawers documented for later reconciliation per W850
Responsible (R): All Staff / Safety Officer / Security
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5538_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5538_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5538_Task13" name="PNP-EOD coordination &amp; scene control">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: PNP-EOD coordination &amp; scene control: security hands the threat recording, data card, and CCTV snapshot of the caller/receiving area to PNP; PNP-EOD sweep leads; building remains closed and the perimeter held until the formal PNP all-clear; no staff re-entry for any reason before all-clear
Responsible (R): Security Guard / PNP-EOD
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager (site control)
Duration: PNP-led (1–6 hrs)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5538_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5538_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5538_Task14" name="Re-entry &amp; recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Re-entry &amp; recovery: after all-clear — W850 reopening mechanics (cash reconciliation vs Step-4 documentation, cold-chain/product checks at DCs), delayed-transaction customer handling, resume trading; if evacuation was *not* invoked (sweep negative), log the stand-down decision with rationale
Responsible (R): Manager / Cash Office / Duty Supervisors
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–3 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5538_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5538_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5538_Task15" name="Documentation, hoax tracking &amp; review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Documentation, hoax tracking &amp; review: W471 Category-A incident report with the complete threat recording and data card; CCTV preserved per the W471 evidence chain; site threat log updated (recurrence pattern → enhanced mail/screening and PNP liaison); VP Legal assesses harassment/prosecution referral; event debriefed into the W158 drill program
Responsible (R): LP / HR / VP Legal
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5538_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5538_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5538_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5538_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5538_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-314 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Preparedness (PA-24.2).) | - operational: threats are reported to PNP regardless of credibility assessment; credibility is never a reason to withhold notification | - operational: only trained staff sweep, only in their own zones, look-don&#x27;t-touch; any find transfers control to PNP-EOD
Owner: Store Manager / Regional Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5538_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5538_Annotation17" targetRef="W5538_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
