    <bpmn:process id="W_W5570" name="W5570. Gas-Leak Event Response (LPG/Natural-Gas Odor on Premises)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A gas odor is reported inside or adjacent to a BuildRight site: LPG smell at or near the cylinder-exchange cage (VS-175), a leaking appliance or regulator connection, a gas line serving the food concession/vending or hot-water service, or a gas odor migrating from a neighboring premises — before any ignition
Frequency: ~10–25 odor-report events per year chain-wide across ~205 sites; the overwhelming majority are minor (faint smell traced to a cage-adjacent cylinder or appliance) and resolve without evacuation of the full trading floor
Volume: 1 event × the exposure-zone tier (zone closure, partial closure, or full evacuation for 1–4 hours) × responders (Store Manager, security, cage/Store Services, BFP, LPG supplier) × the clearance-reading set that gates reopening
Owner: Store Manager (site command); HSE Manager (protocol owner)
Participants: Security Guard, Store Services Lead (cage operations per VS-175), First Aider (VS-83), Facilities (W650), Regional Manager, LPG supplier emergency-response desk, BFP (fire station), gas utility (where a piped-gas service exists), Corporate Communications (W134/W855 if the event becomes public)
Source: workflow W5570 — Gas-Leak Event Response (LPG/Natural-Gas Odor on Premises)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5570_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5570_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5570_Lane2" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5570_Lane3" name="Store Services Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5570_Lane4" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5570_Lane5" name="HSE Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5570_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5570_Start7" name="A gas odor is reported inside or adjacent to a BuildRight site: LPG smell at or near the…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5570_Task8" name="Odor report &amp; classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Odor report &amp; classification: the report is logged with location, strength, and time; the cage and appliance lines are visually checked from a distance for frost, haze or hiss; the exposure-zone tier is set (zone / partial / full) with the heavier-than-air rule in mind — low areas read the hazard last, not first
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5570_Task9" name="Evacuate the exposure zone">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Evacuate the exposure zone: zone closure at minimum; full evacuation where the odor is strong, the source is unresolved, or the cage line is implicated; customers and staff move up and out (no basement/low-route egress); PWD assistance per the W4400 protocols; assembly upwind
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 5–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5570_Task10" name="Ignition-source ban">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ignition-source ban: in the exposure zone — no light switches, no POS power cycling, no phone flashlights; exterior master kill where the zone is electrical; signage and a physical cordon hold the ban while the event runs
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Facilities
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5570_Task11" name="Isolate the source (trained-only, two-person)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Isolate the source (trained-only, two-person): cage master valve closed per the VS-175 training standard where the cage line is implicated; appliance/regulator valves closed by Facilities; never pursue a leak into a confined space or behind racking — the isolation boundary is where training ends
Responsible (R): Store Services Lead / Facilities
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: 5–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5570_Task12" name="Emergency callout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Emergency callout: BFP notified for any event beyond a faint zone-level trace; the LPG supplier&#x27;s 24-hour emergency desk dispatched for cage/appliance events; the gas utility called where a piped service exists; the W650 Facilities call-out runs in parallel
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5570_Task13" name="Ventilation &amp; clearance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Ventilation &amp; clearance: natural/mechanical ventilation per the supplier/BFP guidance with the zone held empty; gas-detector readings at the floor level taken as the clearance standard; the source is repaired, condemned (W5069 quarantine for cylinders) or isolated pending repair
Responsible (R): Facilities / HSE Manager
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: 1–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5570_Task14" name="Documented reopen gate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Documented reopen gate: trading resumes only when the clearance set is evidenced in the incident case — detector-clear readings + source repaired/condemned/isolated + ventilation standard met + (where BFP attended) BFP clearance recorded; the three-party-gate analog of W5537
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HSE Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: At clearance</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5570_Task15" name="After-action &amp; CAPA">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: After-action &amp; CAPA: the source failure mode is classified (cylinder valve, regulator, appliance, third-party migration) and feeds the CAPA register; cage-standards or appliance-maintenance retrofits route to VS-175/W650; the event timeline folds into the W695 drill rotation
Responsible (R): HSE Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5570_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5570_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5570_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5570_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-314 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Preparedness (PA-24.2).) | - operational: trading resumes only after the documented clearance gate (detector-clear + source disposition + ventilation standard, plus BFP clearance where attended); the ignition-source ban and two-person isolation boundary briefed at every store with a cage; implicated cylinders carry the W5069 quarantine state
Owner: Store Manager (site command); HSE Manager (protocol owner)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5570_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5570_Annotation17" targetRef="W5570_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
